 "equipment_type": "Sensor (CO2 / humidity / temperature / pressure)",
 "applies_to": "TSM400-4-CPTH per the Teracom TSM400-4-CPTH user manual TSM400-4-CPTH-R1.9.",
 "summary": "The TSM400-4-CPTH is a Teracom wall-mount multi-sensor for CO2 (NDIR), temperature, humidity and barometric pressure with Modbus RTU over RS-485. Each value is offered as a float and as a 16-bit integer, in metric and imperial blocks, plus trim registers.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The register table prints both a PDU (wire) address and a logical address (PDU + 40001 for holding registers). 'documented' holds the logical number; the PDU number is what goes in the request, e.g. logical 40101 = PDU 100."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "TSM400-4-CPTH User manual",
  "doc_number": "TSM400-4-CPTH-R1.9",
  "revision_date": "2026-10",
  "url": "https://www.teracomsystems.com/download/tsm400-4-cpth-co2-humidity-and-temperature-multi-sensor/",
  "pages": "pp. 6-7 (Modbus address table)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Addresses are taken from the manual's PDU address column (0-based); the logical column is the same number plus 40001, the holding-register offset the manual states.",
  "All 32-bit values follow the Data order register (PDU 13): 1 = most significant word first (factory default), 2 = least significant word first. The map shows the default, ABCD.",
  "Left out: the 32-bit float/integer test-value registers (PDU 82-95), which only exist to check word order; the 16-bit test values are kept.",
  "Float blocks: PDU 100 (Â°C, hPa), 200 (Â°C, mmHg), 400 (Â°F, hPa), 500 (Â°F, mmHg). Integer blocks: PDU 600, 700, 900, 1000 in the same pattern, temperatures and humidity x100.",
  "The mmHg x100 pressure in integer blocks 700 and 1000 is split into a high and a low word; they are listed as two 16-bit registers as the manual does (value = (high x 65536 + low) / 100).",
  "CO2 automatic self-calibration is switched by PDU 2002 (0 = off, 1 = on).",
  "Readings can be trimmed with the multiplier and offset floats near PDU 2100: corrected = measured x multiplier + offset."
 ],
